4. mpc-engine/Cargo.toml declares Apache-2.0 for the local package. Until
   2026-10-08 its resolved dependency graph (Cargo.lock) contained FIVE
   GPL-3.0-family crates, verified against crates.io on 2026-10-07 by
   scripts/check-license-policy.py: multi-party-ecdsa 0.8.1 (GPL-3.0-or-later),
   centipede 0.3.0 (GPL-3.0), bulletproof-kzen 1.2.0 (GPL-3.0),
   round-based 0.1.7 (GPL-3.0), zk-paillier 0.4.3 (GPL-3.0-or-later).
   Those crates were reachable only through the GG20 trusted-coordinator
   signing path. On 2026-10-08 that path was retired and removed
   (docs/plan/PLAN-001-R2-gg20-retirement.md): the Rust sources that used them,
   the GG20 gRPC surface, and the corresponding Java client were deleted, and
   the dependencies were dropped from Cargo.toml. Re-verification with
   scripts/check-license-policy.py on the post-retirement lockfile reports no
   GPL/AGPL-family crates in mpc-engine; cggmp21 (MIT OR Apache-2.0) is the
   sole threshold-signature stack. This entry is retained as a change record.
   Note the distinction: the cggmp21 chain still brings LGPL-3.0-or-later
   components (rug, gmp-mpfr-sys), which permit proprietary use under
   conditions but carry their own notice/relinking obligations - those remain
   open and are tracked in docs/licensing.md section 5.
   If the dependency graph changes again, re-run the scanner and review before
   distribution.

5. Retain existing source and dependency notices. Before distribution, review
